  "title": "Erdős Problem #643",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $f(n;t)$ be minimal such that if a $t$-uniform hypergraph on $n$ vertices contains at least $f(n;t)$ edges then there must be four edges $A,B,C,D$ such that $ A\\cup B= C\\cup D $ and $ A\\cap B=C\\cap D=\\emptyset. $ Estimate $f(n;t)$ - in particular, is it true that for $t\\geq 3$ $ f(n;t)=(1+o(1))\\binom{n}{t-1}? $ ",
